{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments","id":162391,"title":"The Conspiracies Big Guns - new Endowments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T06:54:03-07:00","id":162391,"title":"The Conspiracies Big Guns - new Endowments","content":"I feel like starting a microproject. Endowments that fit the niche of the Conspiracies big guns, though not too powerful to actually use in play like that earthquake causing skull. In all likelyhood these will be too big and powerful to use in combat and will have weaknesses (set-up time normally) that makes them impractical to use in battle to balance them out.<br /> <br /> I'm aiming for one per Conspiracy, though feel free to chime in with your own or ideas. The current plan is:<br /> <br /> <br /> Advanced Armory - a mostly ordinary Apache gunship.<br /> <br /> Benediction - St Barbra. Call down bolts of lightning from the heavens.<br /> <br /> Castigation - I'll think of something - sadly both demon summoning and transforming into a demon are taken.<br /> <br /> Elixir - A small vial of undetectible poison gas.<br /> <br /> Relic - Jericho horns. Small portable hand held relics that can destroy entire skyscrapers.<br /> <br /> Thaumatechnology - Basically, The Hulk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-08-2014, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T07:04:17-07:00","id":162401,"title":"","content":"Rites du Cheval - Summon Totem (a rank 3-4 spirit).<br /> <br /> Goetic Gospels - The equivalent of Mordenkainen's disjunction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T07:29:55-07:00","id":162409,"title":"","content":"Actually, I remember having an idea for a Relic which is actually a bunch of Promethean parts trapped in a coffin- which create massive Wasteland and Disquiet, ruining whole communities. Sounds like something which could work in here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T07:30:16-07:00","id":162411,"title":"","content":"Saint Barbra's Justice<br /> <br /> When Saint Barbra's father had her executed for converting to Christianity heaven dealt justice in the form of a lighting bolt. Since that day Barbra has been the patron of artilleryman, and the Shadow Congregation call upon her intercession to strike down the works of Satan.<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 Willpower<br /> Action: Extended; Each roll takes ten minutes of praying and chanting.<br /> Dice Pool: Composure + Benediction<br /> Dramatic Failure: A bolt of lightning strikes somewhere nearby. It rarely hurts anyone, but it is usually highly inconvenient.<br /> Failure: No progress is made.<br /> Success: Progress is made towards invoking the blessing.<br /> Exceptional Success: Not only is good progress made, the hunter also gains one additional bolt of lightning, provided they score at least ten successes. This bonus can only apply once per invocation of Saint Barbra's Justice.<br /> <br /> When the roll concludes the hunter fires of several bolts of lightning, rolling Dexterity + Firearms; the first bolt requires ten successes and every other bolt requires five successes. A bolt of lightning does fifteen damage, but has a 15 - Size penalty to hit it's target. However it also does five damage to everything in five yards of the impact and 3 damage to everything in 10 yards. If the player declars they are aiming to hit anywhere within five yards of a target there is no size penalty.<br /> <br /> Anything that takes damage from Saint Barbra's Justice is not only shocked by lighting, they are also spontaneously set alight and saturated with holy energies. If the target has any supernatural or natural reaction to any of these forces, they apply in full.<br /> <br /> Under normal circumstances nothing can be hurt by multiple shots from Saint Barbra's Justice in a single turn. Exceptionally large targets may be an exception, if a priest of the Shadow Congregation wanted to direct lightning bolts at individual guns on a battleship that is legitimate, though a battleship is unlikely to take significant damage from a Benediction.<br /> <br /> The ranges are 500 yards, 1000 yards, and 2000 yards for a long range attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T08:14:16-07:00","id":162419,"title":"","content":"<b>Castigation:</b> Set up a ritual binding circle and open a temporary gate directly into the Pit within it, using the binding circle to prevent the devils from wreaking havoc beyond the circle.<br /> <b>Ink:</b> A full-body back tattoo serves as infrastructure that can be used to draw in and sap demonic energy sources, storing it to supercharge unarmed attacks.<br /> <b>Rites of Denial:</b> A ritual splatter of great quantities of blood (effectively requiring at least one human death) overwhelms a consecrated site, limiting or forbidding unnatural creatures to feed from human blood or expend Vitae for mystic actions within the site.<br /> <b>Teleinformatics:</b> Duplicate the talents of a killer by temporarily opening yourself to his psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T09:45:53-07:00","id":162481,"title":"","content":"I'm not feeling an Apache gunship Kings, especially since those suckers are (1) damn expensive to field, and (2) Kinda noticeable in your average city. How about a disguised helicopter in civilian markings with some weapons and gear inside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T10:21:32-07:00","id":162494,"title":"","content":"Expensive is in theme - these are the big guns after all. But I think I can stretch to disguising it as a news helicopter; actually maybe I'll give it some chameleon coating, so that when the power hungry camouflage is turned off it default to black. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Everyone else, good ideas. Get to writing them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the pit might be just the thing to fill in the Castigation gap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-08-2014, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T10:52:24-07:00","id":162524,"title":"","content":"Jericho Horn (OOOOO)<br /> <br /> When the descendants of Abraham arrived at the promised land they discovered that people were already living there. The city states of ancient Canaan fell one by one, and the weapons used to destroy the walls of Jericho have become powerful Relics.<br /> <br /> There are seven Jericho Horns in all, and the Aegis Kai Doru holds them all. The horns are almost too powerful to use, but only almost. When the Shield and Spear has need these powerful and irreplaceable relics are taken into the field.<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Strength + Stamina<br /> Cost: 5 Willpower<br /> Benefit: As anyone who's read the Bible can tell you, Jericho Horns can destroy buildings. All seven combined can tear down an entire city wall, but a smaller number can still cause incredible damage: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Part of a building, such as a gate or front door.</li> <li>An apartment or small family home.</li> <li>A large family home, a church or warehouse, a mansion.</li> <li>A town hall or a similarly sized building.</li> <li>An office complex, or tower block.</li> <li>A shopping mall, sports stadium, a castle or a similar structure.</li> <li>Indefinite size. An entire skyscraper or a city's enclosing walls.</li> </ol><br /> The hunters must walk around the perimeter of the building they wish to destroy once per day for a number of days equal to the horns in use. On the final day they blow a single note, rolling the dice as a teamwork action. If they succeed, and overcome any supernatural protection around the building, the target immediately implodes upon itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-07-2015, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T11:30:02-07:00","id":162571,"title":"","content":"I can't tell you how many story ideas are running in my mind from reading about the Jericho Horns :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T11:37:20-07:00","id":162578,"title":"","content":"Please try, that kind of feedback is my writing fuel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T12:35:03-07:00","id":162605,"title":"","content":"From where could I start? :P<br /> <br /> First, that perhaps the AKD discover a mummies tomb, and that there is a cult which plans to awaken it. They have a week bring down the whole place, which mean avoiding the watchful eyes of the cult as they circle the place and gather all the horns in one place.<br /> <br /> Or maybe someone is stealing the horns one by one, killing their owners and breaking to their Labyrinths. Who would do it and what he wants to destroy that require all the horns together?<br /> <br /> or maybe the MM discover about those legendary artifacts and decide that they are holy relics and should be given to them for they hold the power of God- but how could one steal something which could make the Vatican crumble to dust?<br /> <br /> And what happens when an angel (not necessary the G-M's) show itself before on of the AKD and tells hims about a city that must be destroyed by the help of the horns- and now he need to convince his superiors that he truly needs them?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps someone wish to manipulate the AKD to destroy some structure which interferes with his plans (like, a demon which wants to get rid of an Infrastructure), and so he tries to manipulate the conspiracy to do that for him?<br /> <br /> And just maybe an hunter finds a ritual in which he could intensify the effects of the Horns and do some even crazier things- like. combining them with the Bronze Wheel from Reliquary in order to bring down the Heavens themselves and cast all the angels to earth?<br /> <br /> or another half a dozen ideas which I'm too tired to write :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T14:19:10-07:00","id":162691,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Well lets hope this next one will have the same effect. (BTW, D-IX is a real drug, courtesy of five minuets with Google)<br /> <br /> Double-helIX (OOOOO)<br /> <br /> Among the Nazi occult-research transported to America by Operation Paperclip were lab notes about a drug, D-IX, designed to imbue soldiers with superhuman endurance. Like most Nazi created Endowments D-IX was a Frankenstein of stolen occult lore forced to conform to bullshit Aryan propaganda-myth; it worked, but with such horrific side effects that VALKYRIE left it to rot in a basement after only a token attempt to create a safer version.<br /> <br /> Sometime later Cherion's Field Research division got hold of the notes, with a far greater grasp of pharmaceutical sciences and a more &quot;open minded&quot; attitude about employee safety The Cheiron Group found a way to avoid most of the side effects - because, really, there are limits - and unlock potential in D-IX that it's original creators never dreamed of. They called the resulting mixture Double-helIX.<br /> <br /> Benefit - Double-helIX is no longer pills. The Cheiron Group use retro-viral treatments to modify bone marrow, allowing a field agent to internally produce Double-helIX during times of great stress. When triggered, which requires a point of Willpower and electricity to provide the extra mass (isn't the thaumaturgically enhanced human body an amazing thing?), the Hunter gains five points of both Strength and Stamina as well as a point of Size and Armour as they swell into an over-muscular parody of the human form over the course of an hour.<br /> <br /> While in juiced up on Double-helIX the agent's unarmed attacks count as weapons, with a damage rating of Strength - 5. They may jump (successes) * 5 yards with a strength + Athletics roll. They may use any convient objects with a size lower than their strength as an improvised weapon, it's damage is equal to Size but it also takes as much damage as it deals. Finally, at the end of every turn that they take leathal or aggravated damage, damage roll the damage taken - Composure. On a success increase Strength by one for the remainder of the transformation as stress triggers a further burst of Double-helIX.<br /> <br /> Transforming back requires the agent to spend a point of Willpower and focus on thoughts of calm with a successful Composure role. Getting some time and distance between yourself and your latest rampage usually helps too.<br /> <br /> Special: Chieron has discovered that Double-helIX synergies with a Regenerative Nodule. While amped up an agent my activate the Regenerative Nodule at any time with no cooldown period. He may also substitute an electrical current for food (assume that one Bashing damage from electricity is enough fuel to heal 1/2 bashing, 1/4 Lethal or 1/8 Aggravated damage). When the agent de-transforms the Regenerative Nodule is refreshed.<br /> <br /> Drawback: Oh boy. Aside from turning into a hulking abomination not fit to be seen in the light of day the hunter has to risk spontaneous transformations. Any Dramatic Failure on a Breaking Point or large electric shock will cause the hunter to transform, like it or not. Speaking of Breaking Points, every use of Double-helIX is a breaking point; the chemicals don't just cause the muscles to swell. they also cook the brain to a thick froth. A lower Integrity is only the lasting effects, while juiced up the Hunter is always one step away from a murderous rampage. Any insult or slight requires a successful Composure roll to prevent a murder attempt. Being attacked doesn't even give you a roll.<br /> <br /> It's not entirely a lie to say The Cheiron Group pumps their cannon fodder full of Double-helIX, fires them towards their enemies and watches from a safe distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-14-2014, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:41:27-07:00","id":162792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=162481#post162481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not feeling an Apache gunship Kings, especially since those suckers are (1) damn expensive to field, and (2) Kinda noticeable in your average city. How about a disguised helicopter in civilian markings with some weapons and gear inside?</div> </div> </div> </div>To mirror what was said in the 13th precinct book, few characters have the skills needed to operate a helicopter and when they are up the air, they aren't involved with the rest of the group on the ground. Having such a device would great as an Ally merit but I can't really see it as an Endowment.<br /> <br /> Drones strikes combined with a laser rangefinder would work. Simply deploy the drone high in the sky before doing the work while being personally able to summon down the pain if needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:57:12-07:00","id":162847,"title":"","content":"DARPA is doing some fun stuff with drones connecting to AR head-mounted systems for infantrymen. If you could throw up an eye in the sky that could penalize enemy Stealth rolls, add bonuses to Perception and Firearms pools, identify supernatural creatures, and potentially drop some serious firepower. They're also doing field trials for exoskeletons right now; with the advanced technology of the World of Darkness, that could go some real fun places. Just try not to imagine a Hunter in an exo-rig punching a werewolf's teeth in and you'll see what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> Reality is stranger than fiction, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T14:20:55-07:00","id":164003,"title":"","content":"Oh ye of little faith. 13h precinct is limited by real life helicopters, I am not. There is room for the whole cell in mine. atamajakki, start writing it up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nidhogg Gunship (OOOOOOOOO; the cell may split the cost)<br /> <br /> Durability 6, Size 22, Structure 28, Acceleration 12 (16 mph/turn), Safe Speed 242 (165 mph), Max Speed 293 (200 mph), Handling 1<br /> <br /> When Task Force: VALKYRIE really needs something dead they just blow it up from the sky, sometimes while blasting Flight of the Valkyries. The Force's helicopters are designed for stealth, undercover work and often self-reliance. The kind of major operations where Black Helicopter's are deployed are unpredictable and try as they might those carefully drawn battle plans and chains of command often fall apart. An attack helicopter is too valuable to be deployed without tolerance for chaos. Most have a crew of four.<br /> <br /> A pilot, who's also responsible for the helicopter's primary weapons. Two gunners manning door mounted assault cannons. A communications and sensor's officer, the coms guy is usually the highest ranking person on-board and may find himself taking command if the battle turns chaotic.<br /> <br /> These helicopters are equipped with a large amount of Advanced and conventional military hardware. Foremost of which is the Active Disguise System. Military helicopters are obvious enough as it is, so VALKYRIE use a system of micro-lasers to surround their vehicle with the illusion of a civilian helicopter, the illusions is always larger but you can compensate with a little extra altitude. It doesn't always fool the monsters but it keeps the public ignorant. Sadly the ADS cannot simply display an image of the background, they tried but the result was a distinctly unnatural jellyfish like effect as the ADS lagged behind the helicopter's position. Unless the sky is uniformly coloured the ADS must be used as a disguise and not invisibility. Since the ADS works best when the helicopter's light emittion is minimised, a black coat of paint is standard issue - and rumours arise every time the power hog of a camouflage system is turned off.<br /> <br /> After the camouflage, the bulk of the equipment is dedicated to the coms officer - giving a black helicopter the ability to serve in a surveillance or command role; and the vital ability to find whatever monsters it plans to bomb. They have access to a kirlin camera, an etheric scope, radar, sensors for the full electromagnetic spectrum, a thermal imager, even sonar and advanced noise processing. To communicate they have radio, infra-red, microwave, flashing lights, and even a compartment full of flags that can be hung out of a door.<br /> <br /> The two door mounted heavy automatic cannons are damage eight weapons capable of full autofire, they have a short range of 500 yards, a medium range of 1000 yards and a long range of two thousand yards. They are also armour piercing, ignoring up to six points of armour. The primary weapons are a missile system, which do fourteen points of damage to everything within fifteen yards of the impact point and seven damage to everything in thirty yards. The short range is 5,000 yards, the medium is 10,000 yards and the long range is 20,000 yards. Typically a Black Helicopter is loaded with 16 missiles. It is capable of autofire, but a single medium burst will use the entire payload. Multiple hits stack damage, but it's rare to find a target that can survive even one; but just encase alternative payloads are available. Napalm is the most commonly used.<br /> <br /> Essentially, anything short of a demigod is dead if hit by high grade military ordinance - though it may well get back up again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-15-2014, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T16:48:00-07:00","id":164199,"title":"","content":"fuck. yase. let's write up the big guns. enough of this 'whose the REAL monster' bull... just strain the brain, take a trip to imaginationland and come up with new weapons. my ideas:<br /> <br /> TFV: can you say iron man suit puto? maybe these are real expensive but they should vape most things, which sure seems to fit within the purview of ol task force valkyrie<br /> <br /> Thaumatech: like a failsafe button in your molar or under your eye (so you know it means business). flick or prod that sucker and evolve backwards into a dinosaur. wreck monsters w/ you jaws like a sir <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> elixir: maybe you've read that the assassins (the hassassins back then) were paid in weed? what if the assassins of hunter were paid and controlled w/ ghost crack. this drug should make characters unstoppable and should only be given to the most trill killers<br /> <br /> relic: dragonballs<br /> <br /> benediction: there should be like a secret cathedral that houses like a christian version of the god machine. maybe it can launch nukes that only affect supernaturals via benediction magic or suttin<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:04:38-07:00","id":164293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=164199#post164199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">benediction: there should be like a secret cathedral that houses like a christian version of the god machine. maybe it can launch nukes that only affect supernaturals via benediction magic or suttin</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Dura-Europos Prayer </b>(OOOOO, Relic)<br /> <br /> Early Christians didn't have places of worship like the great Roman temples or crowded Jewish synagogues. Persecuted, hated, and threatened with death, the early Catholic Church would gather in small dwellings and homes. Using secret symbols like the fish they would mark their loyalty and be allowed in to the literal house of worship. The remains of a dwelling in Dura-Europos, Syria, is considered to be the earliest discovered Christian church. One the Malleus Maleficarum guard with such fervor that even the fighting of the Syrian Civil War is kept far away.<br /> <br /> Through intense study, members of the Order of St. Ambrose have uncovered a complex Greek scripture, a benediction that possibly predates all others. Full translation is still years away, and only limited to the team and the Malleus higher ups in the know, but it is quite possibly the most powerful benediction known to the Malleus, for the fact that it calls on an angel to appear to the faithful.<br /> <br /> That's right, angel in the Biblical sense. Sometimes it's reported as a humanoid being of incredible beauty and shape. Sometimes it's a man with the heads of different animals or even a TV. One time the angel was reported as looking way too much like Billy Graham, but it always follows one specific request of the hunter that calls on it. So far the angels summoned have saved local Christians from the violence of the Syrian conflict, produced evidence against pedophile priests, killed entire nests of vampires, and on one occasion gave the requesting hunter the knowledge needed to save a family member from dying of cancer. The angels seem like they can do anything, and that's why the Malleus doesn't want the benediction handed out like candy yet. True, the Malleus are the church's warriors in service to God, but they're also still human. One angel was requested to, &quot;Cut off the cheating bastard's dick&quot;, and well...<br /> <br /> <b>Function: </b>For all intents and purposes, it's an angel. The appearance changes every time the benediction is used, but when properly recited as a prayer the angel appears to those of true faith. (Mechanically, those with Morality/Integrity 9 and up). One request is all the hunter gets before the angel goes away, and no one is willing to try a second time yet for fear of what might happen. But with that one angel, well, as they say. In God, all things are possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:34:46-07:00","id":164312,"title":"","content":"flyboy why are you quoting my idea only to provide a completely unrelated idea. also I think it's very unwise to equate faith with morality/integrity as it implies that one theology is the ticket to sound mind/morals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T20:02:36-07:00","id":164332,"title":"","content":"I think the implication of the description is that they're angels of the God-Machine, or that they might be.<br /> <br /> The Morality/Integrity part could be the Occult Matrix that the Benediction works on. It also might be fair to consider that it isn't actually about Faith at all, though the Malleus might presume that the only people who've thus far been allowed/able to activate it had those Morality/Integrity scores, and they decided it was a sign of how faithful they were.<br /> <br /> Basically, they might be seeing certain people activating it and assume it has something to do with their faith when it really has something to do with their Morality/Integrity. It's funny because, no matter what way you swing it, most Malleus members probably don't have the Integrity/Morality to activate it, so they might need to find people who can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T20:15:05-07:00","id":164339,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the big guns should be a ho har lol at the expense of the conspiracies employing said guns. the big guns should respectfully fuck shit up, for their respective conspiracy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T20:22:45-07:00","id":164348,"title":"","content":"I don't imagine that it is, just that you'd need that exceptional member with the high Integrity/Morality score to use it. Chosen One scenarios and stuff like that come to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:39:13-07:00","id":164526,"title":"","content":"Actually not a GMC style angel, this is just me trying to go with the more traditional, &quot;It's a messenger of God, it doesn't mean the message is good&quot; angle. As I've said before, I don't like the God-Machine angle on angels and demons, I prefer the good ol' fashioned feathery wings and pits of sulfur method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:42:17-07:00","id":164529,"title":"","content":"not me I like the god machine angels. I notice you abbreviate old to &quot;ol'&quot; with an apostrophe, which is an abbreviation which doesn't actually save the user any time while typing. flyboy is this a means you employ towards appearing more 'folksy' in your posts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T23:09:26-07:00","id":164541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=164003#post164003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh ye of little faith. 13h precinct is limited by real life helicopters, I am not. There is room for the whole cell in mine. atamajakki, start writing it up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's mostly a story issue so by all means, let the R&amp;D begin!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V2UGfj2qPCw\" data-code=\"V2UGfj2qPCw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/V2UGfj2qPCw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:23:59-07:00","id":165080,"title":"","content":"Summon an angel; how did I not think of that? Great idea Flyboy, I'm a little unsure of the idea of humans ordering an angel; the other way around seems more Catholic. Maybe have them summon it and hope for the best?<br /> <br /> I'd also give it a stat-block. A Rank 4 or 5 Ephemeral Creature sounds about right. Any more than that and it would be too powerful to give to players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:33:26-07:00","id":165096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=165080#post165080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The other way around seems more Catholic.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're talking to me about what sounds more Catholic, let's dwell on this a sec.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:50:15-07:00","id":165113,"title":"","content":"Well my Jewish background makes me eminently qualified to talk about the spin-off faiths <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, am I wrong to say that humans giving orders to angels is less catholic than humans summoning angels for help and angels doing what they feel is right? It feels against the grain of all the Abrahamic faiths for humans to try and order the divine*; in fact I think that's why there are commandments about taking the Lord's name in vain and graven images.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Which as I mention in the Hakollel thread, is a hidden hint that either the WoD works differently (it is a Promethian focused group) or Hakollel is institutionally sacrilegious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-10-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:07:33-07:00","id":165142,"title":"","content":"Actually, in Catholicism humans are an order above angels, beings with a soul as compared to beings that were created. Remember why Lucifer rebelled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T18:17:53-07:00","id":165460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=165142#post165142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, in Catholicism humans are an order above angels, beings with a soul as compared to beings that were created. Remember why Lucifer rebelled?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the case in some but not all sects<br /> <br /> But anyway, high Morality/Integrity is also indicative of being particularly innocent and sound of soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T02:12:25-07:00","id":167690,"title":"","content":"So- here is an idea I thought about long time ago, and I thought it could be the place to post it :P<br /> <br /> <b>The Faceless Gospel</b> (00000, Geotic Gospels)<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I wish I had an angel,<br /> For one moment of love..<br /> I wish I had your angel,<br /> Your Virgin Mary undone!<br /> I'm in love with my lust,<br /> Burning angel wings to dust!<br /> I wish I had your angel tonight!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> That Gospel is the Knights most secret technique, known only by those who have mastered the dreams of their sleeping gods. In many ways, that Gospel is different from all other Gospels known by the Knights- first, unlike the other Gospels, it is not a number of different powers built upon each other, and instead it is a single, terrifying power (which is represented by by having a fixed, 5 dots price instead of the regular 1-5). Second, while those who lack the understanding of the greater powers behind the Gospel are in danger from learning that power, those who saw the dreams of their Angels are safe, more or less- and instead of breaking their minds entirely, it devours them slowly, piece by piece (so any hunter who doesn't know 5 dots in the other Gospels would gain 1 Persistent Condition per dot beyond 5, those who know 5 dots would not- but instead would suffer an Integrity Breaking Point every time they use the Gospel. Having less than 5 dots in the other Gospels doesn't protect you from treating the use of the Endowment as a Breaking Point.). Finally, unlike the other Gospels, this one doesn't revolve around conquering your Vice and use it as your weapon.<br /> <br /> It is about your Virtues.<br /> <br /> While usually the hunter use himself in order to channel his inner Virtue and fight his demons, in order to sue that Gospel the Knight becomes the &quot;demon&quot; and fight his Virtue, his Angel. However, he must not win that battle, and instead he must humbly allow the Angel to purge his demons out of his body, which burn his soul with searing pain (which is represented by the Price for the Gospel). Once the hunter accept the right of his Virtue to judge his soul, he could call his inner Angel into the world to destroy those who fell victim to their Vices.. and as you can guess, that &quot;Angel&quot; is Faceless.<br /> <br /> The Dots in that Gospel are not considered in order to calculate the number of dice added to Dice Pools which use the Geotic Gospel trait.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Willpower and 1 point of Aggravated Damage (per minute)<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Geotic Gospels<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: the Knight misunderstand the way the Gospel work, and conquer his own Virtue- a thing which must not be done. Not only the Hunter suffer from the Cost as normal, be he also falls into a catatonic state for 24 hours, where his soul travels in the dreams of the Faceless Angels without the protection of his higher self, gaining automatically one Persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> Failure: The hunter lose his internal strife to the Angel, but accept his defeat. Nothing happens.<br /> <br /> Success: The Knight has managed to accept his defeat, and the Angel is manifested, for better or worse. As long as the Angel is present, all magics fail in a radius of 10 meters- spells stop working, relics lose their might, enchantments break apart. Witches may try to resist the effects of the Angelic presence by rolling (Gnosis + Willpower) against the hunter's (Geotic Gospels + Willpower + Faceless Gospel). The presence of the Angel also maddens those who around the Knight- creatures with bestial nature would run away, while sentient beings would suffer from a Breaking Point in their Integrity or their parallel. That include other Knights of Saint George, unless the other Knight has also summoned an Angel. If the Integrity roll is failed, not only the target suffer from the regular effects but would also see a vision of the Angel's true nature- which is never a good thing. The Angel is manifested for a full minute, but the hunter may extend its presence by paying the Cost again, which would give him another minutes every time he does so.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The hunter feels the touch of his Faceless patrons and feel bliss, and the pain is mixed with pleasure. He is gaining the Willpower point paid back (he still suffer from the Aggravated Damage) and need only to suffer from damage in order to maintain the Angelic presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 06-13-2014, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T11:54:02-07:00","id":168123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=165142#post165142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, in Catholicism humans are an order above angels, beings with a soul as compared to beings that were created. Remember why Lucifer rebelled?</div> </div> </div> </div>But still; they're God's messengers. Surely there's something about ordering His people around?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway; this thread isn't actually about Catholic theology <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the ultimate assassination tool for a Conspiracy of assassins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nergal's Feather (OOOOOOO) <br /> <br /> At terrible risk the Ascending Ones stole into heaven and cut a single tumour from Nergal, the Mesopotamian god of war and pestilence. They keep it in their most secret temples and constantly destroy parts of the ever growing lump of flesh. If some elders have their way they would destroy it utterly, out of duty to life itself and to prevent someone else from justifiably destroying the Ascending Ones in their righteous crusade to destroy the heavenly tumour. These elders do not have their way, the Ascending Ones preserve their most potent weapon, and on some occasions they even make use of it.<br /> <br /> Using Nergal's Feather requires no alchemical secrets or self-purification. Just place it and wait for a plague of literal heavenly proportions to fall upon your enemy. The skill is to only harm your enemies, the best Alchemists in the world prepare an Elixir which is injected into the tumour to destroy the divine flesh. Over time the elixir grows more potent, until it eventually overcomes Nergal's flesh and the plague is cut of at it's source.<br /> <br /> Effect: The Ascending Ones need only place a vial of Nergal's Feather somewhere where their foes gather. Once the sealant dissolves everyone who spends time in the same room as the hidden vial takes damage from a Toxicity 7 poison once per hour. To resist roll Stamina + Potency, and any damage inflicted is Resistant. After a week the divine tumour is destroyed, ending the effects.<br /> <br /> Nergal's Feather is completely orderless and symtoms do not manifest for seven days. As a divine pestilence it effects everything. The undead are easy, Nergal's Feather can infect steel robots, clay golem and even incorporeal beings. <b>Everything</b> is susceptible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T22:01:09-07:00","id":172441,"title":"","content":"The Nidhogg Device (00000)<br /> <br /> Durability 2, Size 1.<br /> <br /> About the size of the Witch Buster and bit more fragile, the Nidhogg Device has two modes of operation. The first mode is break it up and attach the bits into the weaponry. Once attached, the device allows the Cell to use a Resolve + Composure + 5 to resist magical attacks on their weaponry.<br /> <br /> The second mode is the creation of a Barren. Upon activation on this setting, the Nidhogg Device creates a Barren for around one square mile. The effect is felt immediately but it does stop all essence production in the area in the Shadow. Give it a few days though..<br /> <br /> Drawbacks: prolonged exposure to the Nidhogg device creates irrational behavior in people. aggressiveness, mental instability, and the like all start to appear after a while. For every hour while in the affected zone or using the weaponry with the components, roll Resolve + Composure. Upon failure, the effected individual is hit with the Irrational derangement that persists until the person leaves the area or ceases contact with the firearm with the device attached.<br /> <br /> There is a bigger version (about the size of a table with the same durability) that just past the prototype phase and is currently in it's first production one that if deployed, will starve 20 square miles of essence. This version is 000000 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T23:01:14-07:00","id":172498,"title":"","content":"<b>Hell Within</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradise Lost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mind is its' own place, and in itself/ can make a heav'n of hell, a hell of heav'n</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradise Lost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me miserable! which way shall I fly/Infinite wrath and infinite despair?/Which way I fly is hell; myself am hell;/And in the lowest deep a lower deep,/Still threat\u2019ning to devour me, opens wide,/To which the hell I suffer seems a heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>A close reading of <i>Paradise Lost</i> presents an interesting notion: That Lucifer is alone in Hell, and that all the other demons are merely his own delusions, and those scenes of hell are nothing more than a broken mind praising itself, arguing with itself, yelling at itself. This isn't the only place an idea like that occurs-modern psychology often explains monsters and spirits and demons as reflections of a person's neurosis. The Lucifuge know this isn't true, as they truck with demons, vampires, fairies, and more everyday.<br /> <br /> But those close to the Lady Lucifuge know it isn't entirely untrue either.<br /> <br /> This castigation is a deeply held secret, because while all of the Lucifuge carry with them and unleash Hell, this one runs the risk of dragging not only the Children of the Seventh Generation off to the burning lakes of darkness, but all others with them. Still, it is perhaps one of the greatest trump cards the demon-blooded can pull, as they drag all into the depths of Hell and render all equal in the darkness where nothing can be seen, and truth is a matter of voice.<br /> <br /> Mechanics coming tomorrow. SPOILER: Hell really does make everyone equal, but it doesn't let go of anyone easily.<br /> <br /> PS: Got an idea for an Ink Big Gun called The Windows of Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-18-2014, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T02:19:10-07:00","id":172559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A close reading of <i>Paradise Lost</i> presents an interesting notion: That Lucifer is alone in Hell, and that all the other demons are merely his own delusions, and those scenes of hell are nothing more than a broken mind praising itself, arguing with itself, yelling at itself. This isn't the only place an idea like that occurs-modern psychology often explains monsters and spirits and demons as reflections of a person's neurosis. The Lucifuge know this isn't true, as they truck with demons, vampires, fairies, and more everyday.<br /> <br /> But those close to the Lady Lucifuge know it isn't entirely untrue either. </div> </div> </div>Maybe both theories are true, in a way. Maybe those demons are born from Lucifer\u00b4s fragmented psyche, like the Wyrm OWoD spawned Urges from his insanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T02:50:12-07:00","id":196164,"title":"","content":"Lets finish the set.<br /> <br /> Castigation: Hell on Earth<br /> <br /> The ultimate power of the Lucifuge opens forth the gates of Hell and lets the damned legions pour forth without mercy. The Lucifuge must create an unbroken circle of iron, then they must cut out their own heart and throw it into the pit while proclaiming it a gift to an archdemon.<br /> <br /> Cost: Surprisingly cutting out your own heart isn't fatal. Instead it inflicts one resistant Aggravated damage that can only be healed with a heart transplant, but if you want to use a new heart as your own for mystical purposes like using this Castigation again you'll need a contract of ownership signed by the donor (however if you see some benefit to living without relying on a muscle to pump blood, feel free).<br /> <br /> Dicepool: Presence + Resolve<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The Archdemon claims both the Lucifuge's heart, and their soul. Inevitably the first thing they'll command their new slave to do is to cut the iron circle allowing the demonic horde free reign upon earth until the portal is destroyed (see below).<br /> <br /> Failure: The castigation fails to activate, unfortunately that includes the part that keeps you alive without a heart.<br /> <br /> Success: The Lcifuge's heart burns with the heat of the Inferno itself, melting it's way through the Earth and opening a passageway into hell. A host of demons subservient to the invoked Archdemon eagerly ascend to wreck havoc, though none may cross the iron circle. At any one time (Castigation + 10 - integrity) x 3 Infernal Rank worth of demons may be active at one time and each demon has a maximum rank of Castigation. If one demon is slain, another eagerly takes it's place. There's only one way to end the flow: Destroy the heart that now lies on the border between Earth and Hell (Size 8, Durability 3, Structure 11). For this reason strategic placement of the heart is vital, too well hidden and the Lucifuge may not be able to end their own weapon, too obvious and the Lucifuge's enemies may well survive the night.<br /> <br /> While within the iron circle demons may fully materialise as an instant action for no cost and do not suffer any essence bleed. Once the heart is destroyed all the usual rules apply, the demons are not banished from Earth but may still lack the power to remain.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Treat Castigation as one dot higher when calculating the total ranks of demons present on Earth at any one time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-28-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T02:26:45-07:00","id":197722,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of the Black Helicopter, but it doesn't really fit the Norse naming theme of the the Conspiracy. Maybe rename it the Nidhogg and trade out for ENE designed missiles? Warheads full of Silver nitrate for the werewolves, high powered &quot;solar&quot; missiles for vampires, a &quot;rust&quot; missile for those pesky arcadians; all things that the Task Force could use and keep the public in the dark. Less full on destruction and more let's end the ENE threat as fast as possible. Could load each Nidhogg with 4 missile types and just carpet bomb the area without creating needless security breaches. Added benefit is that you create a bunch of smaller endowments that Agents could invest in as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;No ma'am, that wasn't a missile, or an explosion, it was a meteor swarm crashing to earth. No, that gas was nothing to worry about, likely a pocket rupturing inside of the meteorite. The gas made your son sick? Well Ma'am, we will send someone over right away to make sure he's ok. No, we won't send you any sort of bill. Thank you for your cooperation Ma'am.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T10:04:00-07:00","id":198021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=197722#post197722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea of the Black Helicopter, but it doesn't really fit the Norse naming theme of the the Conspiracy. Maybe rename it the Nidhogg</div> </div> </div> </div> I never object to people improving on my mediocre ability to name things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/162391-the-conspiracies-big-guns-new-endowments?p=197722#post197722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and trade out for ENE designed missiles?</div> </div> </div> </div> One of the things I really like about this is that a perfectly ordinary standard issue US Army missile is more dangerous to Werewolves than a silver bullet. I think that fits Hunter's theme as the power splat, the biggest and most dangerous things are regular human weapons (case in point - nukes) and Advanced Amory is more portable or tactically useful but not more powerful.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's possible to make effective silver weapons that combine with a typical missile, (I know fire based ones are possible), but given how few monsters could survive even one hit I don't think developing one is going to be TF:V priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}